     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve recently coded in STAN an example of state-space surplus-production model using Meyer-Millar (1999) BUGS in Bayesian stock assessments.</div><div><br></div><div>See attached WinBUGS code for comparison:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"color:#800\">#State-space surplus production model for albacore tuna with lognormal errors</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#############################################################################</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model surplustuna </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">######distribution of I&#39;s#####</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Imean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                 I<